		},
		{
			"file":"4 Misc/Attachments/Pasted image 20241229092326.png",
			"id":"0a9af9613993ee61",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"type":"file",
			"x":4895,
			"y":-3160,
			"width":313,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"9b3d9f01be194fa7",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"# Side Projects\n\n- [ ] solving an orbital mechanics problem numerically (gravitational force + radiation pressure force) and analyze using dynamical systems methods.\n- [ ] Evolving a distribution in phase space\n- [ ] solving the ray equation numerically\n- [ ] Real about [Capacitance & Grounding](Capacitance%20&%20Grounding.md)\n- [ ] Explore the propagation of pulses in dielectric media as opposed to metals.\n\t- [ ] Figure out the amplitude of an EMP pulse\n\t- [ ] understand, given the amplitude of a pulse, how thick would metal walls (Faraday cage) have to be in order to provide protection\n- [ ] A code that takes daily food intake in grams (over a week) and returns average daily distribution of food as well as weekly macronutrient distribution and micronutrient amounts relative to recommended daily amounts. Also - fat profile (omega3 to omega6 ratios, and types of fats consumed saturated, monounsaturated and polyunsaturated).\n- [ ] Error propagation for \"non-differentiable\" functions (e.g functions that are made in function).\n- [ ] **Dynamical Billiards** - implementation attempt using the ray equation and seeing if maybe a complex refractive index can mimic a metal and result in specular reflection.\n\n- [ ] 2D gas in discrete cells\n- [ ] OOP - make the particle an object?\n\t- [ ] each cell (state) can occupy one molecule at a time\n\t- [ ] time evolution\n\t- [ ] reaching equilibrium\n\t- [ ] assessing entropy\n\n- [ ] Modes of coupled oscillators can be excited given the right frequencies. In principle - the more DOFs such a system has the more available resonant frequencies for exciting the modes of the system. Does an infinite chain of coupled oscillators have infinite number of modes?\n- [ ] Physics of lightning bolts\n- [ ] [Ultra Violet Index](../../2%20Puzzles/Ultra%20Violet%20Index.md)\n- [ ] Solving the wave equation numerically on a general boundary (perhaps created by Bezier curves).\n",
			"type":"text",
			"x":5258,
			"y":-2290,
			"width":520,
			"height":2020,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"088064024390d6fe",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"text":"- [Lecture 2 - Resonance II](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TcvY8Nt0ZGA&list=PLUl4u3cNGP62FPGcyFJkzhqq9c5cHCK32&index=3&ab_channel=MITOpenCourseWare)\n\t- [Q factor (Wikipedia)](https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Q_factor)\n\t- [Whispering Gallery Modes ( Wikipedia)](https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Whispering-gallery_wave)\n\t- A comparison between a 2-level system and the QHO. The two systems behave the same in the approximation of weak driving.\n\t- He said that if one excites a QHO, naturally states will \"leak\" to higher levels. This allegedly happens when the driving is not weak and the approximation between the two system no longer holds.\n\t- Two level system - can be saturated, a QHO can be driven to arbitrarily high energies.",
			"type":"text",
			"x":2581,
			"y":-240,
			"width":1080,
			"height":960
		},
